# Template for the local pattern file of bin/check-leaks.
#
# Copy it to the place the tool reads and fill it in:
#
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/trilobit
#   cp .check-leaks.local.example ~/.config/trilobit/check-leaks.local
#
# This template is committed. The file you create from it is not, and it is
# not listed in any ignore file either - it simply does not live inside the
# repository. A committed list of forbidden words would be a list of the very
# things it is meant to hide, and git would keep it forever.
#
# One pattern per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
# Matching is a case-insensitive substring, so a fragment is enough and it is
# found inside identifiers too, which is where such things usually slip in.
#
# What belongs here:
#   - fragments of paths to source trees that are not yours to publish
#   - names of the projects and companies you work for
#   - class names, table names and domain terms taken from those projects
#
# Invented examples, to show the shape - delete them:
#
#   acme-legacy
#   /srv/clients/acme
#   WidgetInvoiceFacade
#
# The file must not be empty: an empty list would let everything through while
# the run still looked green, so the tool exits with code 2 in that case too.
